              "label": "Workspace contributions 1",
              "before": "Run `tests/communityWorkspaceClient.test.cjs` with TypeScript available, `tests/communityWorkspaceDatabase.test.cjs` with PGlite installed, and `tests/communityWorkspace.browser.cjs` with Playwright/Chromium/React UMD fixtures. Use `MAPILLARY_TYPESCRIPT`, `MAPILLARY_PGLITE`, `MAPILLARY_PLAYWRIGHT`, `CHROMIUM_PATH`, `REACT_UMD_PATH`, `REACT_DOM_UMD_PATH` for nonstandard dependency paths. No test contacts a real service. Deploying the SQL requires a separate operator action and real-provider validation.\n\nCreation is a trusted capability distinct from project roles. Existing operators upgrade with `tools/community-notes/migrations/002-collaboration-creator.sql`; client fallback for the trusted legacy key is intentional and never reads user-editable metadata. The original educator-specific SQL is frozen only in a migration test fixture.\n",
              "after": "Run `tests/communityWorkspaceClient.test.cjs` with TypeScript available, `tests/communityWorkspaceDatabase.test.cjs` with PGlite installed, and `tests/communityWorkspace.browser.cjs` with Playwright/Chromium/React UMD fixtures. Use `MAPILLARY_TYPESCRIPT`, `MAPILLARY_PGLITE`, `MAPILLARY_PLAYWRIGHT`, `CHROMIUM_PATH`, `REACT_UMD_PATH`, `REACT_DOM_UMD_PATH` for nonstandard dependency paths. No test contacts a real service. Deploying the SQL requires a separate operator action and real-provider validation.\n\nCreation is a trusted capability distinct from project roles. Existing operators upgrade with `tools/community-notes/migrations/002-collaboration-creator.sql`; client fallback for the trusted legacy key is intentional and never reads user-editable metadata. The original educator-specific SQL is frozen only in a migration test fixture.\n\n## General contribution discovery\n\nMigration 003 adds owner-defined, colored categories and exact workspace queries/statistics. `useWorkspaceContributions.ts` owns independent, abortable read generations and 250 ms server-search debounce. `WorkspaceCategoryEditor.tsx` and `WorkspaceContributionTools.tsx` keep taxonomy and discovery UI separate from auth/member/write orchestration. The panel sends authorized loaded results through `onMapNotes` to the existing map owner; credentials never cross that callback. All loaded authors are drawn automatically. Map/list paging is explicit (50 records), with accurate full-workspace totals and matching counts. Existing risks are legacy read-only data in the UI; normal assignments use owner categories.\n\nSee `docs/WORKSPACE-CONTRIBUTIONS.md` for installation, semantics, limits and the complete contributor map. Refresh is explicit; this does not add polling or ambient service traffic. Category authorization/retirement and statistics membership remain server-enforced.\n"
