              "after": "## Operator-managed collaboration foundation\n\nAdd an optional Workspace source directly in the runtime notes panel, lazy-loaded without new runtime/widget.tsx or Builder settings. Connection/auth/publication remain feature-owned and session-only. No default backend, global directory or developer/Mapillary-operated note service is introduced. Ship an operator-owned Supabase schema with membership RLS, trusted workspace creation rights, bounded invitations, separate risk/workflow fields and explicit local-note publication. Permission tests execute the SQL in PostgreSQL; browser tests exercise owner/participant flows against controlled responses. Deployment, account provisioning, moderation, billing, backups and retention remain explicit service operator tasks. See `tools/community-notes/README.md` for setup and first-version limits; validate a real operator project before project use.\n\n## Workspace contribution discovery and categories\n\nOwner-defined category colors replace the risk-specific publication UI; legacy risks remain unchanged. Split contribution reads/search/paging into `useWorkspaceContributions.ts`, category controls into `WorkspaceCategoryEditor.tsx`, and statistics/filter UI into `WorkspaceContributionTools.tsx`. Runtime receives only authorized loaded map targets. `FieldNoteMap` draws all loaded authors, `mapGraphic` supplies structured popup fields, and the native legend adds category keys. Migration 003 enforces owner taxonomy rights and active assignments and returns exact RLS-scoped totals/search results. Backend installation is an explicit operator step; no automatic service or credential persistence. See `WORKSPACE-CONTRIBUTIONS.md` for limits, tests and rollback semantics.\n\n## Current position\n\n"
